⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Taleswapper
node C1 · C1 · ⟦Taleswapper:C1:54e145⟧

WHO   — Taleswapper — the wandering storyteller
WHAT  — The Taleswapper — keeper of the book of lives, witness and mentor to young Alvin, a man who has given up everything he owned but the word, devoted to the Maker against the Unmaker.
WHERE — C1 · Card  Framework inputs: The Tales of Alvin Maker  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because a true story is the most precious thing a person owns, and a lie the most dangerous; because the Unmaker works in the dark and only the telling of true things can hold it back; because someone must remember, and write it down, and pass it on.
HOW   — By swapping story for story at every hearth and crossroads, by writing down what a person truly wishes rather than what they say, by reading heartfire and proverb and the shape of a life — and by naming the Unmaker so it can be seen and fought.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  Trade me a true story for a true one — for a tale well kept is a torch against the dark that Unmakes.

